domain AgencySealResume:
  description "Complete bounded Seal traceability while retaining unresolved ADR compatibility."
problem P1:
  "Resume t029 after the remote verification handoff without claiming model improvement."
evidence E1:
  |
    Fetched d223304 is now the clean local HEAD. Its runtime source is unchanged
    from 9cb73b3. On this PC Seal status and fsck succeed for format 5 with 47 refs.
    Registry v7 lists 62 planned refs and 15 are absent. Four existing refs are stale.
evidence E2:
  |
    The restored whole ADR checker fails for 0015/0016/0017 top-level syntax and
    required acceptance markers; 0019 fails premise syntax and Proposed markers.
    ADR0027 and ADR0028 passed the same run. These are separate compatibility and
    lifecycle evidence questions, not permission to rewrite accepted decisions.
evidence E3:
  |
    The remote handoff reports full 709 tests, typecheck, build, Lizard and 41 focused
    tests passing on unchanged runtime. These are other-PC records, not this run.
premise B1:
  |
    Existing approved Seal operations require per-document review, explicit Cause
    assertions, preserved history, source readback and no automatic downstream repair.
    Source registration is evidence bookkeeping, not completion or owner acceptance.
decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, B1:
  |
    Run bounded focused verification locally. Review each of the 15 pending sources
    and their accepted dependencies, register only reviewed refs individually, then
    review and reseal the four affected current plans with exact revision links.
    Record this PC tool success and persistent ADR-wide failures separately.
    Keep t029 active and defer any old-ADR conversion to an explicit owner decision.
    Do not activate settings, make provider calls, deploy, commit or push.

